{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00194",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.5,
      "end_seconds": 4.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Excuse me, you know, doctor, should I sit here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.29,
      "end_seconds": 8.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "That's alright, take a seat. Tell me why you've come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.44,
      "end_seconds": 15.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Um, so... red scaly patches on my elbows. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.47,
      "end_seconds": 18.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.8,
      "end_seconds": 49.68,
      "duration_seconds": 27.88,
      "text": "For about a month, I'd say. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me. Okay, so I've had itching too, for two years. Yeah, I've had stiff fingers in the morning too, for nearly five years. About stiff fingers in the morning, maybe a five out of ten on a bad day. It happens a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.76,
      "end_seconds": 52.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "So, have you had pitted nails?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.34,
      "end_seconds": 54.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Yeah, that too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.39,
      "end_seconds": 61.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "Have you had red scaly patches on your elbows before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.3,
      "end_seconds": 68.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened last winter, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.54,
      "end_seconds": 73.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Any new medicines, weeping or sore throat before it started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.03,
      "end_seconds": 77.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Yeah, no, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.37,
      "end_seconds": 80.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Alright, and fever, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.06,
      "end_seconds": 86.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Hmm, uh, not at all, no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.04,
      "end_seconds": 90.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.61,
      "end_seconds": 92.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.14,
      "end_seconds": 95.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.42,
      "end_seconds": 99.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 99.7,
      "end_seconds": 107.88,
      "duration_seconds": 8.18,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pressure 109 over 81, SpO2 98 percent on room air, heart rate 79. Temperature 36.6."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.48,
      "end_seconds": 113.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.02,
      "end_seconds": 132.29,
      "duration_seconds": 17.27,
      "text": "Yeah, not really, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.8,
      "end_seconds": 135.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Let's go through your medication. What are you taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.3,
      "end_seconds": 143.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.09,
      "text": "I mean, it's glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast. Ramipril. I take it 5 milligrams, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 144.68,
      "end_seconds": 149.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 2.5 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.94,
      "end_seconds": 154.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Right. Do you happen to have the current prescription here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.39,
      "end_seconds": 159.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "I, I don't think I have it with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.03,
      "end_seconds": 163.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Let me double-check something in your record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.01,
      "end_seconds": 167.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Hmm, of course, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.32,
      "end_seconds": 185.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Any long-term health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.34,
      "end_seconds": 195.05,
      "duration_seconds": 8.71,
      "text": "I've got diabetes. High blood pressure, for about a year. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.31,
      "end_seconds": 205.73,
      "duration_seconds": 9.42,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known high blood pressure. We'll keep that in mind today. Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.23,
      "end_seconds": 209.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Um, yes, I'm allergic to dust."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.13,
      "end_seconds": 224.38,
      "duration_seconds": 14.25,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.88,
      "end_seconds": 230.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Okay, so good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.72,
      "end_seconds": 234.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.37,
      "end_seconds": 237.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "I'll just listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.05,
      "end_seconds": 255.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Well-defined thick silvery plaques over both elbows and knees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.48,
      "end_seconds": 257.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Open wide for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.8,
      "end_seconds": 279.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "A few small pits in the fingernails."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.47,
      "end_seconds": 281.17,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.66,
      "end_seconds": 298.32,
      "duration_seconds": 13.66,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. So, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is plaque psoriasis. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I'd also keep eczema in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.45,
      "end_seconds": 301.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "Doctor, is this dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.76,
      "end_seconds": 319.2,
      "duration_seconds": 16.44,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with plaque psoriasis do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had red scaly patches on your elbows for about a month, and no weeping or sore throat before it started."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.8,
      "end_seconds": 321.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.26,
      "end_seconds": 338.18,
      "duration_seconds": 14.92,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 339.05,
      "end_seconds": 341.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.37,
      "end_seconds": 350.23,
      "duration_seconds": 7.86,
      "text": "Let's get blood tests, for baseline before treatment. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.98,
      "end_seconds": 354.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.59,
      "end_seconds": 376.52,
      "duration_seconds": 21.93,
      "text": "Let's use calcipotriol-betamethasone gel, once a day, for four weeks. That's for psoriasis. A little sunlight helps psoriasis, but avoid sunburn. Moisturise often. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 377.12,
      "end_seconds": 378.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.46,
      "end_seconds": 388.38,
      "duration_seconds": 8.92,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency. Let's review you in four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 389.97,
      "end_seconds": 391.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 392.26,
      "end_seconds": 397.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Can you run through the plan with me quickly, just to be certain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 397.72,
      "end_seconds": 406.09,
      "duration_seconds": 8.37,
      "text": "So, I take the calcipotriol-betamethasone gel, once a day and come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 407.03,
      "end_seconds": 411.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Take care, and don't hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 412.31,
      "end_seconds": 414.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Uh, no questions. Thank you."
    }
  ]
}